From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kanadaj <kanadaj@royalroad.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:46:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Don't crash the PipelineRun Logs tab while the PipelineRun
 loads

The details page can render the Logs tab once with obj undefined. Every
other read of obj in PipelineRunLogs uses optional chaining, but the
Pod watch built obj.metadata.namespace, so the tab intermittently showed
"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'metadata')" (two of three
loads of a finished PipelineRun on a kind cluster).

Backport of the same line from upstream main (b9e1cd7, "cve: manual
cherry-pick of SRVKP-13295"); drop this patch once release-5.0 has it.
---
 src/components/pipelineRuns-details/PipelineRunLogs.tsx | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/components/pipelineRuns-details/PipelineRunLogs.tsx b/src/components/pipelineRuns-details/PipelineRunLogs.tsx
index 06fc033..e56ea56 100644
--- a/src/components/pipelineRuns-details/PipelineRunLogs.tsx
+++ b/src/components/pipelineRuns-details/PipelineRunLogs.tsx
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@ const PipelineRunLogs: FC<PipelineRunLogsProps> = ({
     podName && {
       name: podName,
       kind: 'Pod',
-      namespace: obj.metadata.namespace,
+      namespace: obj?.metadata?.namespace,
       isList: false,
     };
   const waitingForPods = obj && activeRun?.kind === 'TaskRun' && !resources;
